@@ -48,3 +48,7 @@ Choose one USB device in the launcher's **Sharing** pane, and Omarchy gets it at
 - **Hubs can't be passed through.**
 - **The device is tied to its port.** If you move it to another port, choose it again.
 - **Keep it plugged in while Omarchy runs.** Unplugging it can freeze the window for up to 30 seconds.
+
+## SSH in an embedding manager
+
+Omarchy VM Manager offers **Enable SSH from this Mac** when creating a guest. Once normal owner-account setup finishes, its SSH page verifies the connection and offers **Copy SSH Command**. Each guest has a separate localhost port and pinned identity. An optional public key selected during creation can also log in; the manager never copies your private key. A host-key mismatch stops verification and requires reviewed recovery. The normal Try Omarchy app's manual SSH setup above is unchanged.
